{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass at the end of forty days, etc., HaShem gave me.</b> From here they learned that on the very day the tablets were given, on that same day the calf was made, for when he mentioned above ״ויתן ה׳ אלי״ he did not specify on which day; therefore he returned and specified here, ״at the end of forty days.״ And this is what Isaiah said, of blessed memory (Isaiah 17:11 [11]): ״ביום נטעך תשגשגי״ — from the language of סיגים (dross), and it is the sin of the calf; and thus Targum Jonathan rendered: באתר דאתקדשתון למהוי עם תמן קלקלתון עובדיכון — 'in the place where you were sanctified to be a people, there you corrupted your deeds.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The verse cited as Isaiah 17:11 is in the received text Isaiah 17:11; the Hebrew reads י״ז:י״א which is 17:11 — apparently a formatting variant. The wordplay on תשגשגי / סיגים follows the midrashic reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:05.264870342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}